From 3f41ca220bb6e905f7f5af8b5398790f9dee0444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:35:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] apu: send the VP/DSP output block instead of wiping it

mcpx_apu_monitor_frame cleared frame_buf before mixing the test tone and
the DirectSound software mixer into it, so everything the VP and the DSP
passthrough wrote over the last 8 frames was discarded: titles using
hardware voices were silent. The monitor now sends frame_buf with the
tone/mixer added on top and clears it afterwards (as xemu does).

Rate: one 256-sample block per EP frame. XAudio2 buffers are now 256
samples with up to 16 queued and 4 silent blocks prefilled when the
queue runs dry (counted as starved in RECOMP_APU_STATS); before, each
call sent 1,024 samples and 3 of 4 were refused. waveOut collects 8
blocks per 2,048-sample buffer instead of rendering 2,048 per block.

RECOMP_APU_MONITOR=vp sets monitor.point to MON_VP (the VP's L/R voice
sum, xemu's default without DSPs) for A/B against the mixbin mixdown.
The apu_mixdown test now also checks the monitor block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
